  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالشَّمْسِ وَضُحٰٮهَاۙ‏(1)\nWASH SHAMSE WA ZOHAAHAA.\nBy the sun and her forenoon splendour,\nوَالْقَمَرِ اِذَا تَلٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(2)\nWAL QAMARE EZAA TALAAHAA.\nby the moon when he follows her,\nوَالنَّهَارِ اِذَا جَلّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(3)\nWAN NAHAARE EZAA JALLAAHAA.\nby the day when it reveals her,\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا يَغْشٰٮهَا ۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA YAGHSHAAHAA.\nby the night when it covers her,\nوَالسَّمَآءِ وَمَا بَنٰٮهَا ۙ‏(5)\nWAS SAMAAA-E WA MAA BANAAHAA.\nby the sky and Him who built it,\nوَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا طَحٰٮهَا ۙ‏(6)\nWAL ARZE WA MAA TAHAAHAA.\nby the earth and Him who spread it,\nوَنَفْسٍ وَّمَا سَوّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(7)\nWA NAFSINW WA MAA SAWWAAHAA.\nby the soul and Him who fashioned it,\nفَاَلْهَمَهَا فُجُوْرَهَا وَتَقْوٰٮهَا ۙ‏(8)\nFA-ALHAMAHAA FOJOORAHAA WA TAQWAAHAA.\nand inspired it with [discernment between] its virtues and vices:\nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ مَنْ زَكّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(9)\nQAD AFLAHA MAN ZAKKAAHAA.\none who purifies it is felicitous,\nوَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ دَسّٰٮهَا ؕ‏(10)\nWA QAD KHAABA MAN DASSAAHAA.\nand one who betrays it fails.\nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ بِطَغْوٰٮهَآ  ۙ‏(11)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO BE-TAGHWAAHAA.\nThe [people of] Thamud denied [Allah’s signs] out of their rebellion,\nاِذِ انْۢبَعَثَ اَشْقٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(12)\nEZIM BA-A’SA ASHQAAHAA.\nwhen the most wretched of them rose up.\nفَقَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ نَاقَةَ اللّٰهِ وَسُقْيٰهَا ؕ‏(13)\nFAQAALA LAHUM RASOOLUL LAAHE NAAQATAL LAAHE WA SUQYAAHAA.\nThe apostle of Allah had told them, ‘This is Allah’s she-camel, let her drink!’\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَعَقَرُوْهَا  ۙفَدَمْدَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِذَنْۢبِهِمْ فَسَوّٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(14)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-A’QAROOHAA, FA-DAMDAMA A’LAYHIM RABBOHUM BE-ZAMBEHIM FASAWWAAHAA.\nBut they impugned him and hamstrung her. So their Lord took them unawares by night because of their sin, and levelled it.\nوَلَا يَخَافُ عُقْبٰهَا‏(15)\nWA LAA YAKHAAFO UQBAAHAA.\nAnd He does not fear its outcome.",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Makki’ Surah and has 15 verse. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (S) that the reward for reciting this Surah is compared to the things upon which the sun and the moon shine.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that the person who recites Surah as-Shams, al-Layl, az-Zoha and al-Insherah will, on the Day of Judgement, find all creatures of the earth testifying on his behalf and Allah will accept their testimony and give him a place in Jannah. Recitation of this Surah also leads to an increase in sustenance, courage and popularity amongst the people."
